  "problem": "Let $F(x)=4x-1$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,6)$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x+12)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nII. $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n\nIII. $f(x+3)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$",
